    "title": "Brownsville mechanic arrested for unauthorized use of patrol unit - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shirley Escobedo ,\n4 hours ago\nBROWNSVILLE, Texas ( ValleyCentral ) — A 32-year-old was arrested on Wednesday for unauthorized use of a marked Port Isabel Police Department patrol unit, according to the Brownsville Police Department.\nFollowing an investigation into the patrol unit being left for repairs at Nieto’s Auto Shop, located at 2200 E. 14th St. in Brownsville, investigators discovered that Daniel Nieto had operated the patrol unit around the city.\n( Daniel Nieto, Photo Courtesy of Brownsville Police Department )\nBrownsville PD says the investigation also revealed Nieto would activate the patrol unit’s overhead lights and sirens while hanging out with friends.\nNieto was arraigned and issued a $7,000 bond.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KVEO-TV.",
